<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	Privacy manifest for the Runner (app) target only.

	This declares required-reason API usage for THIS APP'S OWN Swift code
	(ios/Runner/*.swift — the AlarmKit MethodChannel bridge and its App
	Intent). It intentionally does NOT attempt to declare usage on behalf of
	third-party CocoaPods/SwiftPM dependencies: Apple-maintained Flutter
	plugins that touch required-reason APIs (e.g. shared_preferences,
	path_provider, device_info_plus) ship their own PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy
	inside their own frameworks/pods, which Apple's tooling merges with this
	one at archive time. Adding speculative declarations here for APIs this
	target's own code never calls would misrepresent actual usage.

	Audited usage (see ios/Runner/AlarmKitPlugin.swift and
	AnswerPrayerAlarmIntent.swift):
	  - UserDefaults.standard is read/written/removed to bridge the AlarmKit
	    "Answer" action's pending payload, and to track scheduled AlarmKit
	    alarm IDs, entirely within this app (no App Group, no shared
	    container) -> NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults, reason
	    CA92.1 ("access info that is only accessible to the app itself").
	  - No file-timestamp, disk-space, system-boot-time, or active-keyboard
	    required-reason APIs are called anywhere in this target's own code
	    (verified by search — no FileManager attribute/timestamp reads, no
	    ProcessInfo.systemUptime/mach_absolute_time, no volume-capacity
	    queries, no UITextInputMode/activeInputModes usage), so those four
	    categories are deliberately omitted rather than declared "just in
	    case".

	This app collects no data of its own (no analytics, no tracking, no
	network account, no ad SDKs — see lib/screens/privacy_policy_screen.dart)
	so NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes is empty and NSPrivacyTracking is false.
	-->
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>CA92.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
